<div class="sec" id="s7">
  <div class="num">07</div>
  <h2>Cheat sheet</h2>
  <div class="cheat">
    <h3>Getting going with AI: cheat sheet</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Which window?</div>
        <p>
          Claude chat prepares a request. Claude Code builds the website. Your
          browser checks it. Delta is optional.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Start again</div>
        <p>
          Open a terminal, use <code>cd</code> to enter your project folder and run
          <code>claude --permission-mode default</code>. See <a href="#s3"
            >setup</a
          > for the exact steps.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">A new job</div>
        <p>
          Use the <a href="#s4">prompt writer</a> for a substantial request. Keep
          small corrections in the existing conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Check the result</div>
        <p>
          Open <code>index.html</code>, refresh after edits and check the words,
          photos, email link and narrow layout. Use the <a href="#s5"
            >website checks</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="blk">
        <div class="h">Safety</div>
        <p>
          No secrets. Read the plan. One project folder. Keep a backup. Leave
          Claude Code's permission prompts on; <a href="#s6">Delta has none</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
